{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Listing_Results)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Listing Results)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ruby and Sam each roll a fair 6-sided die with the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87c4f20da2e1950da5c2d2b8fcebab09cb12b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on its faces. Sam subtracts the number on his roll from the number on Ruby’s roll. What is the probability that the result is a negative number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfac139424858b7228e455e1a77767bb3652d7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{5}{18} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{12} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{7}{12} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"398\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Listing_Results.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Listing_Results)\">Solution 1 (Listing Results)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Listing Results)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realise that the result would be negative when the number on Ruby's roll is less than the number on Sam's roll. Additionally, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/0805f8acf15f0b5ef6b52bfac52610c823802f3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r, s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> represent the combination of rolls where Ruby rolls a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and Sam rolls an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba3e3f9bd99ddc2bf9e6d9244ebf4bfbc3776d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1acbf245a710398f64953985490d7b1134630b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5df99ccd1c7c4b384bb2b3a5b9d270c6aa4abf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506b58320deb5004bf2ed2f1a5e3e672d6e326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a601c8e837eafe7d899c2ba96295b3637daf6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6f0e4cd615eb4d118bf243be6594935ad3de9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c86ca1c4b2e0ef486c0cafcf9a2eefffa10421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f47290d3c991aac723270e49b5415eb82b2cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea44bd62795a5d84c16a028ff4fb079a5cb8e63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04fa1d70044a676ae0a28e1476d5192f5cd8496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9492e0ae17ba8045ad2de885400cf91207e83db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281cb98ef359560b94673052664a637c131ec362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1924ac42c8e1d1cb79000224acbe2c46d4b22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347741cade420c9172f1251847efddfdeb489ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ad99fd4eff7c80182e09559fe59f36b5844e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b148ef6cc1c0ce3aebeede22fd06969a213bd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190d53edddf17fdf15d88488290c282a150354d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5c05123d72c760159fe732b683014c75008c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e45c55a387ecd0ff1c5c07aa081bdcd9a7fbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1cf8a9e18c3e06c87c6bb9840782dc4c7828a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf953fb2c072b3fd3f9daad973c7e1ee5fc53aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b6a364920ec84c82c57831adffe0e2ad2b9be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b5a7c6dea205547307d7f8a9f35366c15b819d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0994ca0283f051e07f29844f7af73f4624eef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e936447969453c86785fddfee03c502514fa298f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a6aa4fae2c4e4c29b43f57a15cd214e525e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0429617bc1afa148bd90f2912e2e3f0a85c98ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd1499dbb1ea032542c13537a2ca2f157d4c832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of which have Ruby's roll less than Sam's roll.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the result being a negative number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f3b0359c3c4859c4a7cdddd50ae978c0d8626c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba75235594d8eff825a3c510d168c42f5d46411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can start by realising that the result would be negative when the number on Sam's roll is greater than the number on Ruby's roll.\n</p><p>The number of possibilities of rolls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities when each person rolls the dice.\n</p><p>We can split the problem into different cases based on the number on Ruby's roll.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam can get a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498538e0c5e486e73a341926ae724fdff91776ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 2 + 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam can get a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1c859d994882f18c595de1bcc6f1bc89c5f9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 3 + 1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam can get a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a651e5a0348a8dce840be185b947a641594c918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 4 + 1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam can get either a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam can get a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibility.\n</p><p>If Ruby gets a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, Sam cannot go any higher, so there are no possibilities.\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have also realised that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less case each time because each time the number on Ruby's roll is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less value that Sam's roll could've been for the conditions to be met.\n</p><p>There would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d54c6bbbab6fd22310a33c0caea7304fe3a2982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 0 = \\frac{5 \\times 6}{2} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"38\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the result being a negative number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f3b0359c3c4859c4a7cdddd50ae978c0d8626c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba75235594d8eff825a3c510d168c42f5d46411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 2, we can start by realising that the result would be negative when the number on Sam's roll is greater than the number on Ruby's roll and that the total number of possibilities is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities where the numbers are equal to each other, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4028e4e459cafdcae55791faeb09a518a6506a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 - 6 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities where the numbers are not equal to each other.\n</p><p>The probability of the number that Sam rolled being greater than the number that Ruby rolled is the same as the probability of the number that Ruby rolled being greater than the number that Sam rolled because each dice has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability for each number, so it would be symmetrical between the two. This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68cae02fedbd39268572c8d44ec69d95e3e8dd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{2} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> possibilities where the number on Sam's roll is greater than the number on Ruby's roll.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the result being a negative number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f3b0359c3c4859c4a7cdddd50ae978c0d8626c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba75235594d8eff825a3c510d168c42f5d46411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resourc